    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, CURRENT] Reviewed 2026-11-01 on dev 100b6fbb6e. hypergumbo run on one JS file: el.innerHTML=r and el.outerHTML=r emit no edge, new Function(r)() and setTimeout(r,1)/setInterval(r,1) emit no edge, el.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',r) emits javascript:external:0-0:insertAdjacentHTML; document.write/eval controls reach their sinks (violated). New since filing: b2ee3ebd65 (INV-pivam/INV-rorur, 2026-09-29) added unreached: lists to dom_injection.yaml/code_execution.yaml, so a clean verdict now says confirmed_with_caveats with unreached_sink_shapes naming all four shapes. The recall gap itself is unchanged. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nRESIDUAL of WI-nokab (PR #1301, ADR-0060), filed on closing it. taint now SHIPS code_execution and dom_injection sinks (taint_sinks/), but four JS/TS injection shapes still reach no sink because the analyzer emits no usable edge for them. Measured on dev bfdead0700 with one function reading document.referrer:\n- el.innerHTML = r / el.outerHTML = r: an ASSIGNMENT to a property -- no edge of any type (the WI-zumoz class). The most common DOM-XSS sink.\n- el.insertAdjacentHTML(\"beforeend\", r): emitted, but as javascript:external:0-0:insertAdjacentHTML (untyped receiver, call_construct=method), so a row would match any project method of that name by short name alone; not rowed.\n- new Function(r)(): no edge.\n- setTimeout(r, 1) / setInterval(r, 1) with a string: no edge (JS_KNOWN_GLOBAL_CALLS holds fetch and eval only); a string and a function argument are one call shape, so an edge would need the argument's type to be a sink.\nEach needs analyzer reach first, then a row in taint_sinks/{code_execution,dom_injection}.yaml. test_shipped_taint_sinks keeps any such row out of the I/O-derived zones."  # 9f93
